Cut 2026-10-23 on Anthony's word ("Merge 792 and the follow on steps for release"; the tag push stays his), in PR release/v0.91.0. A minor carrying:
- #785-#788 (P7, a hub on one machine): search_design and compose_and_analyse take tracked_designs and reach every design a hub pins by its committed export, through --call too; a hit opens with get_node on its prefixed id; one composed check over a hub and several designs (other_graph_ids, by_design, by_pair, across); computed seams (computed_links, candidates, link_status, set_aside); import_graph merge and properties_removed; upstream_status reviewed_revision and record_state; link_far_end_stale;
- #789: rmcp 3.6.0 (its new 16 MiB line bound lifted on stdio and the --call pipe; HTTP keeps 4 MiB);
- #790 (PR A1): bridge premise, EQUIVALENT_TO, circular steps, a proof read as a proof whatever its domain, contested through a contested contradiction, a what-if walks through falsum;
- #791 (PR A2): claimed_by reads claimed; status over time and withdrawn; not_read sources and source grades on Artifact; a refreshed mirror keeps what its source withdraws (superseded, reason-lost, accept_withdrawal); replaced judgments read superseded; independence compares premises; unsourced objections contest only;
- #792 (PR B): premise reasons said once (premise_whys), hub replies held to budget, get_skill and propagate_from take budget_chars (default 30,000), --call prints compact JSON.

200 tools, as in 0.90.0; measured against the published 0.90.0 binary, eleven tools differ (add_artifact, add_requirement, add_constraint, add_inference, compose_and_analyse, search_design, import_graph, mirror_surface, get_skill, propagate_from, pair_designs); 34 skills (design-a-proof, design-an-argument, hub, adopt, impact-check, link-projects bodies changed); get_instructions gains one section. THE SCHEMA STAMP MOVES (edge type EQUIVALENT_TO, 68 -> 69; statement_kind bridge; Artifact source_reliability and information_credibility), so docs/upgrading-to-v0.91.0.md is owed and written, measured with the published 0.90.0 binary: 0.90.0 refuses any store 0.91.0 has opened, even read-only; every seat upgrades together. Nothing is deprecated or removed. Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Xbw6PG9mXJiU2Sb421fnq
